# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# Without this file EAS falls back to .gitignore — and that fallback reads the
# root file only, not nested ones. `apps/mobile/.gitignore` ignores `/android`,
# so git never showed the local Gradle output there, but every build shipped it:
# 3.9GB on disk, a 1.2GB archive, and an upload this connection reset partway
# through every time. The native sources are a few hundred KB; the rest is
# output the build server regenerates.
#
# This file REPLACES .gitignore for uploads, so everything that one excludes has
# to be repeated here. Keep the two in step.

# Dependencies — installed on the build server.
node_modules

# Native projects. This app is Continuous Native Generation — app.config.js is
# the source of truth and EAS runs prebuild itself, which is why Expo's own
# apps/mobile/.gitignore ignores /android. The directory on this machine is the
# leftover of a local `expo run:android` for the emulator, and it must not be
# uploaded: EAS would treat it as a bare project and take its versionCode 1
# instead of the counter it keeps, which is how the last three releases were
# numbered 6, 7 and 8.
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios

# The web app's public assets and the repo's documentation. Both are tracked,
# and neither is an input to an Android build — the mobile app ships its own
# artwork under apps/mobile/assets. Together they were 35MB of an 87MB upload,
# on a connection that resets partway through one this size.
public
docs

# Expo, Next.js and tooling caches.
.expo
apps/mobile/.expo
.next
.next-dev
.turbo
dist
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Test and report output.
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
*.log

# Local database files.
data/*.db
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal

# Downloaded EAS artifacts — the reason .gitignore mentions the upload at all.
builds/

# Deployment and secrets. Build-time values come from eas.json and EAS
# environment variables, never from a file in the archive.
.vercel
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Claude Code agent tooling.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json
